#~ msgid ""
#~ "The name HIM DUB draws its roots"
#~ " from a defining moment in African"
#~ " history: the joint coronation of "
#~ "Emperor Haile Selassie I and Empress "
#~ "Menen Asfaw on 2 November 1930, in"
#~ " Addis Ababa. It was an extraordinary"
#~ " event, delegations from 72 nations "
#~ "travelled to witness it, and a "
#~ "powerful symbol of balance between "
#~ "masculine and feminine energy, joined in"
#~ " leadership."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "The name HIM DUB draws its roots"
#~ " from a defining moment in African"
#~ " history: the joint coronation of "
#~ "Emperor Haile Selassie I and Empress "
#~ "Menen Asfaw on 2 November 1930, in"
#~ " Addis Ababa. It was an extraordinary"
#~ " event, delegations from 72 nations "
#~ "travelled to witness it, and a "
#~ "powerful symbol of balance between "
#~ "masculine and feminine energy, joined in"
#~ " leadership."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Haile Selassie's 44-year reign left a"
#~ " lasting mark on the 20th century."
#~ " He pushed through sweeping modernisation,"
#~ " abolished slavery, introduced Ethiopia's "
#~ "first written constitution, and became a"
#~ " vocal advocate for human rights, "
#~ "self-determination, and nuclear disarmament "
#~ "on the world stage. He was a "
#~ "founding figure of the Organisation of"
#~ " African Unity and played a key "
#~ "role in the creation of the United"
#~ " Nations. His legacy also runs deep"
#~ " through Rastafari, where he is "
#~ "regarded as a central spiritual figure,"
#~ " one of the many threads that "
#~ "ties our name back to the roots"
#~ " of reggae culture itself."
